     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough. Without it, the attacker can always win: phishing gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. Escalating the workstation, or the lack of segmentation, allows pivot_internal. MFA on users is bypassed from the workstation foothold, so auth_appserver succeeds, and kerberoasting then yields stolen_admin. With mfa_admin deployed, auth_dc and auth_adfs are both blocked, so foothold_dc, foothold_adfs, admin_dc and admin_adfs are unreachable. stolen_dbadmin can only come from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, so it is unobtainable. auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup all require stolen_dbadmin, so no admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup can be reached, and exfiltration is impossible. Zero controls is insufficient, so the minimum is 1.\"}"
    }
   ],
